<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jasper Tudor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1431–<a href="/years/1495">1495</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Jasper Tudor, Duke of Bedford</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jasper Tudor was a Welsh nobleman, half-brother of Henry VI and earl of Pembroke, who was a leading Lancastrian commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>. He protected his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england">Henry Tudor</a>, born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pembroke-castle">Pembroke Castle</a> in 1457, and shared his exile in Brittany. After Henry won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bosworth-field">Battle of Bosworth</a> in 1485 and became Henry VII, Jasper was made Duke of Bedford.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jasper-tudor.jpg" alt="Jasper Tudor" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Sauber · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cardiff_castle_-_Eingangshalle_1b_Erkerfenster.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
